                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[b]Played Character Route Order: Joey ◈ Quinn ◈ Trinity ◈ Leia[/b]\n\n[i][b]Valentine Panic[/b][/i], developed and published by [b]Michaela Laws[/b], known as the creator of [url=https://store.steampowered.com/app/367120/Seduce_Me_the_Otome/]Seduce Me the Otome[/url] among other titles, is a cute and fully voiced Memory/Visual Novel hybrid, which is worth a look if you want to pass time. Although the game includes Visual Novel as well as romance elements, the romance and storyline are so paper-thin that I suppose this should not be your main reason to buy it. Keep in mind that you'll spend 90% of the time playing memory. I'm not particularly looking for memory games per se, but I felt entertained for the one hour it took me to collect every achievement. Additionally, and in case you are a memory enthusiast ([i]Is that even a thing?[/i]), you can also give the endless mode a try.\n\nhttps://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=1213481378\n\nHere is a brief summary of the story: our nameless and genderless protagonist is, [i]without much success[/i], looking for a job when they suddenly get a call with the offer to work in a cafe. Once working there, we can pursue two male and two female characters. The conversations between the main character and the romance interests are more of a friendly than flirtatious nature, though. I was expecting a romantic and fluffy story but that is not really what [i][b]Valentine Panic[/b][/i] offers to the player. It's fluffy for sure but romance is only vaguely hinted at when reaching an ending.\n\nhttps://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=1213481309\n\nOverall, it's a pretty good deal in my opinion for just $0.99, taking into consideration that it is also fully voiced. The story is, even if there isn't much of it in the first place, well written and quite enjoyable.\n\nYou can totally go for it if you can picture yourself liking a memory game in combination with a short and rather uneventful storyline.\n\n[h3][quote]𝐅𝐨𝐥𝐥𝐨𝐰 [url=https://store.steampowered.com/curator/33853800/]𝐎𝐭𝐨𝐦𝐞 𝐒𝐞𝐤𝐚𝐢'𝐬 𝐂𝐮𝐫𝐚𝐭𝐨𝐫 𝐏𝐚𝐠𝐞[/url] 𝐟𝐨𝐫 𝐦𝐨𝐫𝐞 𝐕𝐢𝐬𝐮𝐚𝐥 𝐍𝐨𝐯𝐞𝐥 𝐚𝐧𝐝 𝐉𝐑𝐏𝐆 𝐑𝐞𝐯𝐢𝐞𝐰𝐬[/quote][/h3]",
